go 1.27.2

// The kernel and the wire are developed in this tree and released on their own
// cadence. A workspace is how that happens without a replace directive: the root
// go.mod must stay replace-free, because `go install pkg@version` refuses a module
// that redirects its own dependencies.
//
// A consumer never sees this file — a downloaded module's go.work is ignored — so
// the published artefact builds against the published tags. CI runs one job with
// GOWORK=off to prove exactly that, which is also what catches pin drift.
use (
	.
	./platform
	./protocol
)
